# [ST09-I S5.7-6] Explicit admission phase transition across the
# release boundary. A place route's certificate covers carrying legs,
# the release boundary, and unloaded retreat — but the UNLOADED phase
# is only activated AFTER the release side effect is verified:
#   CARRYING phase -> release side effect -> detach confirmed ->
#   activate UNLOADED phase -> retreat executes.
# The caller (driver) owns the release effect and its evidence; the
# certifier side owns the verdict and refuses by name otherwise.
string route_digest
string certification_id
string target_phase
# Vacuum-off was accepted AND the state machine confirmed detach.
bool detach_confirmed
# Release evidence identity (vacuum command echo / event id).
string release_evidence
# Map revision observed after the release (0 = not yet advanced).
uint64 map_revision_after_release
---
bool success
string reason_code
string detail
